From: FlaxAdvisors
Subject: Fix SEGV in ipmi_sen_get_sdr when no YAML sensors are defined

When the compiled sensor table is empty (no sensor YAML files provided),
ipmi_sen_get_sdr assigns sensors.end() to the 'sensor' iterator and then
proceeds to dereference it unconditionally, causing a SEGV via
populate_record_from_dbus -> isAnalogSensor when ipmitool sends Get SDR 0.

Return SENSOR_INVALID immediately when the table is empty so the caller
gets a clean error response instead of a crash.

--- a/sensorhandler.cpp
+++ b/sensorhandler.cpp
@@ -1334,6 +1334,11 @@
     // the call.
     auto sensor = ipmi::sensor::sensors.begin();
     auto recordID = get_sdr::request::get_record_id(req);
+    if (sensor == ipmi::sensor::sensors.end())
+    {
+        *data_len = 0;
+        return IPMI_CC_SENSOR_INVALID;
+    }

     // At the beginning of a scan, the host side will send us id=0.
     if (recordID != 0)
